<%# The signed-in person's two notes settings AS STORED, for `admin--notes--alert`
    on <body> (its `settings` target). <body> lives as long as the tab -- CS
    Studio moves between screens inside `#content` -- so the values written
    on it with the page went stale the moment the account screen saved new
    ones, in that tab and in every other. This element is what the save's
    answer replaces (a stream, `Admin::AccountsController#update_profile`):
    the controller takes the values from it as it connects and tells the
    person's other tabs. In the layout it says what <body> says. %>
<%= tag.span id: "notes-alert-settings", hidden: true,
      data: { "admin--notes--alert-target": "settings", sound: (Current.user&.notes_sound ? true : false), desktop: (Current.user&.notes_desktop ? true : false) } %>
